## 6. API Service Layer Pattern

```typescript
// services/rfqService.ts
const API = import.meta.env.VITE_API_URL;

export const rfqService = {
  getAll:    (filters?) => fetch(`${API}/rfq?${new URLSearchParams(filters)}`),
  getById:   (id: number) => fetch(`${API}/rfq/${id}`),
  create:    (data: CreateRFQPayload) =>
               fetch(`${API}/rfq`, { method: 'POST', body: JSON.stringify(data) }),
  update:    (id: number, data: UpdateRFQPayload) =>
               fetch(`${API}/rfq/${id}`, { method: 'PUT', body: JSON.stringify(data) }),
  cancel:    (id: number) =>
               fetch(`${API}/rfq/${id}/cancel`, { method: 'PATCH' }),
  compare:   (id: number) => fetch(`${API}/rfq/${id}/compare`),
  award:     (id: number, vendorId: number) =>
               fetch(`${API}/rfq/${id}/award`, { method: 'POST', body: JSON.stringify({ vendorId }) }),
};
```

**Service files needed:**
- authService — login, logout, refresh token
- rfqService — CRUD + compare + award
- quotationService — submit, list by RFQ
- vendorService — CRUD + performance
- poService — CRUD + send to vendor + PDF
- approvalService — inbox, approve/reject, config levels
- documentService — upload, list, download
- notificationService — list, mark read
- auditService — list with filters + export
- adminService — users CRUD, roles, permissions

