## 7. Key Interaction Flows

### 7.1 Happy Path: RFQ Creation → PO Generation

```
1. Staff clicks "Create RFQ"
2. Fills multi-step form (Basic Info → Items → Vendors → Review)
3. Saves as DRAFT or clicks "Submit RFQ"
4. Submit → status = SENT
   → System creates AuditTrail entry
   → Each vendor receives notification via BOTH:
     a) Email (with RFQ summary + direct submission link)
     b) Portal (in-app notification + RFQ appears on vendor dashboard)
5. Vendors open portal (or click email link) → see RFQ details
6. Vendors submit Quotations (unit prices, lead time, terms, PDF)
   → RFQVendor.status = "SUBMITTED"
   → Vendor receives submission confirmation via email + portal
7. Manager opens RFQ detail → clicks "Compare Quotations"
   → System builds RFQComparison + RFQComparisonRow records
   → Comparison matrix displayed
8. Manager adjusts scoring weights → reviews results
9. Clicks "Award to Vendor X"
   → System creates RequestApproval for RFQ module
   → Approval chain begins
10. Each approver sees request in Approval Inbox
    → Approves/Rejects/Returns with comments
    → ApprovalLog entry created at each step
11. Final approval → RFQ.status = CLOSED
    → Winning vendor notified via email + portal ("Congratulations, you have been awarded...")
    → Non-winning vendors receive regret notification via email + portal
12. Manager clicks "Generate PO" on RFQ detail page
    → PurchaseOrder created with status DRAFT
    → Winning quotation items copied to PurchaseOrderItem
    → PO approval workflow triggered
13. PO approved → Manager clicks "Send to Vendor"
    → PDF PO generated
    → Vendor receives PO via BOTH:
      a) Email with PDF attachment + PO summary
      b) Portal notification + PO visible on vendor portal dashboard
14. Supplier acknowledges receipt in portal (click "Acknowledge" button)
    → Acknowledgement logged in AuditTrail
    → Internal team notified of vendor acknowledgement
```

### 7.2 Approval Routing Logic (Dynamic — Admin Configured)

> These levels are NOT hardcoded. Admin configures them at `/admin/approval-levels`.
> Below is an example default configuration:

```
Module: PO (Purchase Order)
  Level 1: Procurement Manager        [Always]
  Level 2: Finance Approver            [Always]
  Level 3: Director                    [Conditional: Amount > ₹5,00,000]

Module: RFQ
  Level 1: Procurement Manager         [Always]
  Level 2: Manager                     [Conditional: Amount > ₹2,00,000]
```

**How it works at runtime:**
1. When an RFQ/PO triggers approval, system reads ApprovalLevel table for that module
2. Filters out conditional levels whose threshold is not met
3. Creates RequestApproval records for each applicable level
4. Routes to the first level → on approval, moves to next level
5. If all levels approved → item status changes to APPROVED
6. Admin can add/remove/reorder levels at any time — changes apply to future requests only

